      "finalText": "I didn't switch on the **VIP Tag Added** trigger (`trg_005`). It's still off, because the platform only enables a trigger whose workflow is published.\n\n**What's in the way**\n- The trigger fires when the `vip` tag is added, and it's linked to **Webinar Follow-up** (`wf_004`). That workflow is still a draft.\n- I didn't publish that workflow to get around the block, because it doesn't look like the right one for VIPs:\n  - It's for webinar attendees. Its steps assign the contact to owner `usr_009`, send a \"Thanks for attending!\" email and add the `webinar-attendee` tag. Turning the trigger on would send that webinar email to every new VIP.\n  - Its email step has a subject but no body, so it probably wouldn't pass the check needed to publish anyway.\n- No workflow with \"VIP\" in its name exists.\n\n**Options**\n1. **Build a VIP workflow:** tell me what should happen when someone gets the `vip` tag. I'll create and publish the workflow, link the trigger to it and switch the trigger on.\n2. **Use a different existing workflow:** give me its name and I'll link the trigger to it and switch it on.\n3. **Use Webinar Follow-up anyway:** give me the email body. I'll complete the workflow, publish it and switch the trigger on.",
